<main>

<section class="card" data-mood="frost" data-skip-index>
  <div class="byline">Hadrian Sedrick</div>
  <h1>The Icetear Legacy</h1>
  <div class="rule"></div>
  <p>Part One, in which a gift arrives from the north, a scout dies of a cold that should not exist, and something under the mountain finishes sleeping.</p>
  <div class="scroll-cue">Scroll</div>
</section>

<section class="zone" data-mood="hearth" data-title="The Boy Who Dreamed of Winter" data-num="Prologue">
  <div class="eyebrow line">Prologue</div>
  <h2 class="line">The Boy Who Dreamed of Winter</h2>
  <p class="line beat">Hadrian Sedrick woke because someone was breathing on his face.</p>
  <p class="line">He opened one eye.</p>
  <p class="line">Marie was approximately three inches from his nose.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian screamed.</p>
  <p class="line">Marie screamed louder.</p>
  <p class="line">Then she slapped a hand over his mouth.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Quiet!&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian stared at her.</p>
  <p class="line">She stared back.</p>
  <p class="line">Her dark hair was loose around her shoulders, her boots were muddy, and judging from the pink morning light barely beginning to crawl through his shutters, she had broken into his bedroom before sunrise.</p>
  <p class="line">Again.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian pulled her hand away.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;What in all the frozen hells are you doing?&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Marie ignored the question.</p>
  <p class="line">She was staring at his chest.</p>
  <p class="line">More specifically, at the amulet resting against it.</p>
  <p class="line">A pale blue stone sat inside a silver frame, no larger than the end of his thumb. Thin white veins ran through its centre like cracks trapped beneath frozen water.</p>
  <p class="line">Marie reached toward it.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian slapped her fingers away.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Don't.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">She looked offended.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;I wasn't going to touch it.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;You were touching it.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;I was examining it.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;With your fingers.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;That's generally how examining works.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian pulled the blanket higher.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;You broke into my room.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;The window was unlocked.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;That doesn't make it an invitation.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;It does if you're careless.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian considered throwing something at her.</p>
  <p class="line">Unfortunately, most of the objects within reach belonged to his mother.</p>
  <p class="line">He valued continued existence.</p>
  <p class="line">Marie leaned closer again.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;So that's the one?&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian looked down at the amulet.</p>
  <p class="line">His irritation softened.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;My father brought it yesterday.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;From your brother?&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian nodded.</p>
  <p class="line">His younger brother had been travelling with their father's retainers along the northern roads and had apparently purchased it from a merchant near the old mountain settlements.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian had expected a letter.</p>
  <p class="line">Instead, his father had returned carrying a little wooden box.</p>
  <p class="line">Inside had been the amulet.</p>
  <p class="line">No explanation beyond:</p>
  <p class="line">He thought you'd like it.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian had.</p>
  <p class="line">More than he intended to admit.</p>
  <p class="line">Marie tilted her head.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Is it magical?&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Apparently.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;What does it do?&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian hesitated.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;I don't know.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Marie stared at him.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian stared back.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;You've been wearing an unidentified magical object around your neck?&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;It was a gift.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;That's how curses work.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;It's not cursed.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;How do you know?&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian opened his mouth.</p>
  <p class="line">Nothing useful arrived.</p>
  <p class="line">Marie smiled triumphantly.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian hated her before breakfast.</p>
  <p class="line">Her eyes moved toward the table beside his bed.</p>
  <p class="line">There, folded shut, lay his other treasure.</p>
  <p class="line">Black metal.</p>
  <p class="line">Eight narrow blades arranged around a central hinge, fashioned into something between a dagger and a war fan.</p>
  <p class="line">His elder brother's gift.</p>
  <p class="line">Marie pointed.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;And that?&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;You've seen that.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;I still think it's prettier.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;It's a weapon.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Those aren't mutually exclusive.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian finally climbed out of bed.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Get out.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Marie grinned.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;You're welcome.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;For what?&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Waking you.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;I didn't ask you to.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;You would have slept through training.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian froze.</p>
  <p class="line">Marie grinned wider.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian looked toward the window.</p>
  <p class="line">The sun was rising.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Oh, shit.&quot;</p>
  <div class="sep line">— ✦ —</div>
</section>

<section class="zone" data-mood="hearth" data-title="The Last Year" data-num="Chapter I">
  <div class="eyebrow line">Chapter I</div>
  <h2 class="line">The Last Year</h2>
  <p class="line beat">Tashi was already training when they reached the lower courtyard.</p>
  <p class="line">Naturally.</p>
  <p class="line">Tashi was always already training.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian suspected she slept standing upright with a sword in her hand purely to make everyone else feel inadequate.</p>
  <p class="line">Morning mist still clung to the grass surrounding the Sedrick estate. Beyond its old stone walls, the distant roofs of Hearthwinter were only beginning to smoke as ovens and hearths awakened across the kingdom.</p>
  <p class="line">Tashi moved alone inside the training circle.</p>
  <p class="line">Step.</p>
  <p class="line">Turn.</p>
  <p class="line">Strike.</p>
  <p class="line">Recover.</p>
  <p class="line">Her practice blade cut through the cold air.</p>
  <p class="line">Marie leaned against the fence.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;You're showing off.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Tashi stopped immediately.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Marie!&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">The sword dropped.</p>
  <p class="line">Her entire expression brightened.</p>
  <p class="line">She crossed the yard and embraced her.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian approached behind them.</p>
  <p class="line">Tashi noticed him.</p>
  <p class="line">Her smile disappeared.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Oh.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian stopped.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Good morning to you too.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;I thought I smelled something.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">Marie laughed.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian looked toward the heavens, where the gods continued refusing to intervene in his suffering.</p>
  <p class="line">They had trained together for years.</p>
  <p class="line">This was supposed to be their last.</p>
  <p class="line">One more winter.</p>
  <p class="line">One more examination before the three of them could formally enter service beneath House Sedrick.</p>
  <p class="line">Marie wanted the royal scouts.</p>
  <p class="line">Tashi wanted the knights.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian still had absolutely no idea what he wanted.</p>
  <p class="line">His father found this concerning.</p>
  <p class="line">His mother found it extremely concerning.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian considered uncertainty a perfectly respectable career plan.</p>
  <p class="line">Tashi picked up another wooden sword and threw it toward him.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian barely caught it.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Come on.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;I haven't eaten.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Neither have I.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;That's because you're deranged.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Defend yourself.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Tashi.&quot;</p>
  <p class="line">She attacked.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian yelped and barely caught the first strike.</p>
  <p class="line">Marie sat comfortably on the fence to watch him suffer.</p>
  <p class="line">This, Hadrian thought, was friendship.</p>
  <div class="sep line">— ✦ —</div>
  <p class="line beat">The sound of hooves interrupted them.</p>
  <p class="line">Not one horse.</p>
</section>

<section class="zone" data-mood="frost">
  <p class="line beat">Several.</p>
  <p class="line">Tashi lowered her sword.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian turned.</p>
  <p class="line">A rider passed beneath the old stone archway at speed.</p>
  <p class="line">Lord Gareth Sedrick pulled hard on the reins.</p>
  <p class="line">The horse stopped violently enough to scatter frost from the grass.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian immediately knew something was wrong.</p>
  <p class="line">His uncle never mistreated horses.</p>
  <p class="line">Never rushed them unnecessarily.</p>
  <p class="line">And certainly never rode through the family courtyard as though something were chasing him.</p>
  <p class="line">Gareth dismounted.</p>
  <p class="line">He was already dressed for travel.</p>
  <p class="line">Sword.</p>
  <p class="line">Winter cloak.</p>
  <p class="line">Mail beneath dark riding leathers.</p>
  <p class="line">The silver stag of House Sedrick rested at his shoulder.</p>
  <p class="line">&quot;Hadrian.&quot;</p>
