<section class="zone" data-mood="frost" data-title="The Cave" data-num="Chapter II">
  <div class="eyebrow line">Chapter II</div>
  <h2 class="line">The Cave</h2>
  <p class="line beat">They rode for nearly four hours.</p>
  <p class="line">Hearthwinter slowly disappeared behind them.</p>
  <p class="line">First the city walls.</p>
  <p class="line">Then farms.</p>
  <p class="line">Then the little villages clustered along the northern road.</p>
  <p class="line">Eventually there was only wilderness.</p>
  <p class="line">Snow thickened beneath the horses.</p>
  <p class="line">The trees became taller.</p>
  <p class="line">Older.</p>
  <p class="line">Quieter.</p>
</section>

<section class="zone" data-mood="dread">
  <p class="line beat">Hadrian had travelled north before.</p>
  <p class="line">Never this far.</p>
  <p class="line">There were stories about these mountains.</p>
  <p class="line">Most were nonsense designed to frighten children.</p>
  <p class="line">Ancient Fae ruins.</p>
  <p class="line">Buried kingdoms.</p>
  <p class="line">Sleeping giants.</p>
  <p class="line struck">White dragons.</p>
  <p class="line">Hadrian had believed exactly none of them.</p>
  <p class="line">Then they reached the cave.</p>
  <p class="line">He stopped believing quite so confidently.</p>
  <p class="line">It lay beneath the side of a mountain, almost invisible beneath accumulated snow.</p>
  <p class="line">Or what had once been a cave.</p>
</section>

<section class="zone" data-mood="dread">
  <p class="line beat">The entrance had collapsed.</p>
